CANHarbor's gs_usb protocol research uses the following fixed reference:

  sorrowfeng/gsusb-canfd
  https://github.com/sorrowfeng/gsusb-canfd
  Commit: 6785cc82d66da93cb3ff5af66a6b3498f1118c66
  Copyright (c) 2026 gsusb-canfd contributors
  License: MIT (full notice in LICENSES/gsusb-canfd-MIT.txt)

Protocol request numbers, feature bits, control response layouts and host-frame
layouts were checked against this reference. CANHarbor's Rust implementation
and synthetic test vectors were written for this project. No C++ implementation,
firmware, Linux kernel driver, binary, or captured CAN traffic is included.
See docs/m1-gsusb.md for source paths, provenance, and scope.

Generated browser validators retain their own bundled dependency notices inline
in web/src/generated/api-validators.js. Cargo.lock and web/bun.lock
identify the dependency versions; this file is not a complete release SBOM.

nusb 0.2.9 (https://github.com/kevinmehall/nusb) is used as a Cargo dependency.
License: MIT OR Apache-2.0; selected MIT. See LICENSES/nusb-MIT.txt.
Transitive platform dependencies and exact versions are recorded in Cargo.lock.

